 token_expires_at = timezone.now() + lifetime, so asking again replaces both. change_password_from_recovery only accepts a token whose token_expires_at is in the future. An expired token, or a legacy token without an expiration date, gets the same 400 'Token is invalid' as an unknown token, and nothing on the user changes. On success the token and its expiration date are cleared. For consistency, change_password, change_email and User.cancel() also clear token_expires_at. The new tests fail on the old code and pass on the new code. The users integration and permission tests pass (84), make check-fast passes (238), and make migrations-check passes. The whole suite was still running when I had to report, so I have no result for it yet. The first attempt with `make test` stopped before running any tests: `make db-up` could not bind port 5432, because another worktree's PostgreSQL container already uses it. I restarted the suite against that same container with a separate test database name, so that I do not clash with another session's test_taiga database.","changes":[{"path":"settings/common.py","summary":"Added PASSWORD_RECOVERY_TOKEN_LIFETIME = timedelta(hours=1)."},{"path":"taiga/users/models.py","summary":"Added nullable DateTimeField token_expires_at; cancel() clears it."},{"path":"taiga/users/migrations/0034_user_token_expires_at.py","summary":"New migration adding User.token_expires_at."},{"path":"taiga/users/api.py","summary":"password_recovery sets token_expires_at. change_password_from_recovery filters on token_expires_at__gt=now() (same 400 error as an unknown token) and clears both fields on success. change_password and change_email also clear token_expires_at."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_users.py","summary":"Added tests: expiration is set from the setting, asking again replaces the token and expiration, a valid token succeeds and clears both fields, the full flow is rejected after the lifetime (mocked now), and expired or legacy tokens are rejected exactly like unknown ones and the user does not change. The max-length recovery test now sets a future expiration."},{"path":"tests/integration/resources_permissions/test_users_resources.py","summary":"The recovery permission test now sets a future token_expires_at."},{"path":"docs/harness/log.md","summary":"Added a 2026-11-02 entry for this change, what was learned, and what is left."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"Recovery tokens expire after the configured time and legacy tokens are rejected like unknown ones","met":true,"evidence":"The new tests test_password_recovery_sets_token_with_expiration, test_change_password_from_recovery_full_flow_and_expiration and test_change_password_from_recovery_rejects_expired_or_legacy_token[expired|legacy-without-expiration] pass. The last test checks that the status and body are the same as for an unknown token and that the password, token and expiration do not change."},{"criterion":"The change is covered by tests","met":true,"evidence":"6 new or changed recovery tests fail against HEAD's api.py (checked by putting the old file back for one run) and pass with the change."},{"criterion":"The existing test suite still passes","met":false,"evidence":"These parts pass: make check-fast (238 passed), tests/integration/test_users.py together with resources_permissions/test_users_resources.py (84 passed), and make migrations-check ('No changes detected'). The whole suite (about 15 min) was still running when I had to report, so I have no result for it. The first `make test` attempt stopped at `make db-up` (port 5432 already allocated) before running any tests."}],"human_needed":[{"question":"Is it acceptable that all recovery tokens issued before the deploy stop working, so that users must request a new recovery email?","why":"The task asks to reject legacy tokens. This affects users who have a recovery email waiting in their inbox at deploy time."},{"question":"Should PASSWORD_RECOVERY_TOKEN_LIFETIME be configurable through an environment variable in docker/config.py?","why":"AGENTS.md says docker/config.py variable names need care, so I did not add one. Today Docker installations can only use the default of one hour."}],"harness_used":["AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md: commands table (make check-fast, migrations-check, test), the conventions on migrations and gettext, and the rule to add a harness log entry","The --create-db versus --reuse-db note in AGENTS.md","docs/harness/log.md format","make db-up / make migrations-check targets"],"harness_gaps":[{"file":"Makefile","problem":"`make test` and `make check` always call `make db-up`, which fails when another worktree's compose PostgreSQL already uses port 5432. There is no way to choose another port or test database name, so parallel worktrees can share and overwrite the same test_taiga database."},{"file":"tests/config.py","problem":"The test database name is fixed, and no environment variable can change it. To isolate the full run I had to write a settings module outside the repo."},{"file":"AGENTS.md","problem":"Nothing says how to run the whole suite when several worktrees run in parallel, or how long it takes without coverage."}]},"ttft_ms":2999,"type":"result","duration_ms":201013,"uuid":"d66aa8e9-e0f5-4761-9c91-bf8381249249","ttft_stream_ms":2125,"time_to_request_ms":146,"first_content_frame_ms":2125,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":56,"outputTokens":11160,"cacheReadInputTokens":1168536,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42186,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7946191999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1039,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":42186,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
