ariable names need care, so I did not add one.\"}],\"harness_used\":[\"AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md commands table (make check-fast, migrations-check, test)\",\"Conventions on migrations and the harness log\",\"The --create-db versus --reuse-db note\",\"docs/harness/log.md format\"],\"harness_gaps\":[{\"file\":\"Makefile\",\"problem\":\"`make test` and `make check` always call `make db-up`, which fails when another worktree's compose PostgreSQL already uses port 5432. There is no way to choose another port or test database name, so parallel worktrees share the same test_taiga database.\"},{\"file\":\"tests/config.py\",\"problem\":\"The test database name is fixed, and no environment variable can change it. I had to write a settings module outside the repo to isolate the full run.\"},{\"file\":\"AGENTS.md\",\"problem\":\"Nothing says how to run the whole suite when several worktrees run in parallel. The suite takes longer than the default 10-minute background limit for agents, and nothing warns about this.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"partial","summary":"Password recovery tokens now expire. There is a new setting, PASSWORD_RECOVERY_TOKEN_LIFETIME, with a default of timedelta(hours=1), and a new nullable field User.token_expires_at with migration 0034. password_recovery sets a new token and token_expires_at = timezone.now() + lifetime, so asking again replaces both. change_password_from_recovery only accepts a token whose expiration is in the future. An expired token, or a legacy token without an expiration date, gets the same 400 'Token is invalid' as an unknown token, and nothing on the user changes. On success the token and its expiration date are cleared. change_password, change_email and User.cancel() also clear token_expires_at. The new tests fail on the old code and pass on the new code. The users integration and permission tests pass (84), make check-fast passes (238), and make migrations-check passes. No full run of the suite has finished yet. The first `make 